Fixed the legacy language server silently discarding every `scan` setting sent in `initializationOptions` — including `configuration`, the user's rule set — whenever that object carried a key the server didn't recognize. Editors send all settings their manifest declares a default for, so an editor knowing about a setting the server didn't (for example `secrets`) caused a fallback to defaults and a scan against the `auto` registry ruleset instead of the configured one. Unrecognized keys are now tolerated, and a parse failure is logged instead of being swallowed.
